1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,790
Elias's paper had his obituary.

2
00:00:03,211 --> 00:00:05,421
It arrived a day
early: his name,

3
00:00:05,511 --> 00:00:08,061
his apartment, a fire at 3:07.

4
00:00:09,258 --> 00:00:10,008
He was alive.

5
00:00:10,894 --> 00:00:11,804
He had no subscription.

6
00:00:11,804 --> 00:00:15,164
Underneath, in small
print: one name per

7
00:00:15,164 --> 00:00:19,363
fire. At 2:40,
Elias knocked on 4A.

8
00:00:19,753 --> 00:00:22,063
Mara's heater had been
sparking all week.

9
00:00:22,700 --> 00:00:24,330
She'd asked him to fix it.

10
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:25,930
He told her to call the super.

11
00:00:26,725 --> 00:00:28,655
He took the stairs
and didn't look

12
00:00:28,655 --> 00:00:31,268
back. From the
hotel, he watched the

13
00:00:31,268 --> 00:00:31,968
smoke rise.

14
00:00:31,968 --> 00:00:35,508
At 3:07, 4B burned.

15
00:00:36,139 --> 00:00:37,649
The next paper
waited at the front

16
00:00:37,649 --> 00:00:39,469
desk. Same fire.

17
00:00:39,799 --> 00:00:40,649
Same hour.

18
00:00:40,859 --> 00:00:41,629
Different name.

19
00:00:42,288 --> 00:00:43,058
Mara Kwan.

20
00:00:43,348 --> 00:00:44,678
Apartment 4A.

21
00:00:45,048 --> 00:00:46,838
It said she'd entered 4B to warn

22
00:00:46,838 --> 00:00:49,881
him. Elias laid the
two obituaries side

23
00:00:49,881 --> 00:00:50,821
by side.

24
00:00:51,171 --> 00:00:51,521
His name.

25
00:00:51,521 --> 00:00:55,822
Mara's. The paper wasn't
predicting the future.

26
00:00:56,566 --> 00:00:58,756
It was choosing who paid for it.
